# Xenomai 4 (EVL) Kernel for ARM64

This kernel tree has Xenomai 4 (EVL) real-time extension with the Dovetail
interrupt pipeline integrated.

## Quick Start

### Prerequisites

- ARM64 cross compiler (aarch64-none-linux-gnu-)
- Standard Linux kernel build dependencies
- meson and ninja (userspace libraries only)

### Build Kernel

```bash
# Using the build script
./build-kernel.sh

# Or manually
export CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-none-linux-gnu-
export ARCH=arm64
rm -f .config .config.old
make LOCALVERSION= defconfig cix.config
make LOCALVERSION= -j$(nproc) Image modules dtbs
make LOCALVERSION= bindeb-pkg  # For DEB packages
```

`LOCALVERSION=` is passed empty so that `scripts/setlocalversion` does not
append a `+` to the release string; the suffix itself comes from
`CONFIG_LOCALVERSION` in `cix.config`.

The script will generate DEB packages under `../xenomai4-out/debs/` (relative to kernel source):
- `linux-image-*.deb` - Kernel image
- `linux-headers-*.deb` - Kernel headers
- `linux-libc-dev_*.deb` - Kernel libc development files

### Build Userspace Libraries (libevl)

```bash
# Using the build script (automatically clones libevl at tag r49)
./build-userspace.sh

# The libevl source will be cloned to ../libevl/ (relative to kernel dir)
# DEB package will be generated at ../xenomai4-out/debs/cix-libevl-xenomai4_4.0.0_arm64.deb
```

The userspace build reads the EVL UAPI headers from `include/uapi/evl/` in this
kernel tree, so run it from this tree (or point `KERNEL_SRC` at it).

### Configuration

`cix.config` sets:

- `CONFIG_IRQ_PIPELINE=y` - Dovetail interrupt pipeline
- `CONFIG_DOVETAIL=y` - Dovetail core
- `CONFIG_EVL=y` - EVL real-time core
- `CONFIG_LOCALVERSION="-cix-xenomai4"` - Kernel version suffix

`build-kernel.sh` verifies the first three after merging the config and aborts
if any of them is missing, so a manual build should check them too.

### Install

```bash
# Install kernel packages on target
dpkg -i linux-image-*.deb linux-headers-*.deb linux-libc-dev_*.deb

# Install Xenomai userspace libraries
dpkg -i cix-libevl-xenomai4_*.deb
```

The Xenomai userspace will be installed under `/usr/xenomai/`:
- Libraries: `/usr/xenomai/lib/`
- Headers: `/usr/xenomai/include/`
- Tools: `/usr/xenomai/bin/`

